    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d367">

                <pb facs="0443" n="369" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav01/pg369"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/1054</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d367-f1"
                    />
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-02-07T22:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 7, 1918, 10 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6491. Embassy Petrograd reports that Kamenev has been
                    appointed Envoy Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary at Large of the <pb
                        facs="0444" n="370" xml:id="pg370"/> Bolshevik government and
                        Zalkind appointed in the same capacity to Switzerland
                    and that passports of both have been visaed by British representatives. Please
                    ascertain if report regarding visa is true.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d367-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d367-f1-content">
                <p>The same, <hi rendition="#italic">mutatis mutandis,</hi> on the same date, to the
                    Ambassador in France (No. 3154).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
